commit 23f02b623a2f92f84e136171dbc3103956b899f0 (HEAD -> dev/nasahlpa/fixconfig, origin/dev/nasahlpa/fixconfig)
Author: Pascal Nasahl <nasahlpa@lowrisc.org>
Date:   Mon Nov 9 09:38:10 2026 +0100

    configs: Fix packed el2_param_t vector when lockstep options are dropped
    
    When lockstep_enable=0 (or lockstep_regfile_enable=0), the lockstep_*
    keys are deleted from %config, so gen_define() never converts their
    %verilog_parms entries to binary and they keep the raw field width
    (e.g. "7"). dump_parms() concatenates these characters into the packed
    parameter vector and b2h() silently turns the affected nibble into 0,
    clearing neighbouring fields. For example, with lockstep_enable=0 and
    load_to_use_plus1=1, pt.LOAD_TO_USE_PLUS1 is 0 although
    RV_LOAD_TO_USE_PLUS1 is defined and the comment block shows 5'h01.
    With lockstep_enable=1 and lockstep_regfile_enable=0,
    pt.LOCKSTEP_ENABLE is 0.
    
    - Zero the %verilog_parms entries of dropped lockstep_* keys
    - Fail in dump_parms() on any non-binary parameter value
    
    Signed-off-by: Pascal Nasahl <nasahlpa@lowrisc.org>
